-- title:
--   Poitou–Tate reciprocity at {∞}∪ S for odd p
-- statement:
--   Fix an odd prime $p$ and a finite set $S$ of rational primes, let $M$ be a representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over $\mathbb Z/p$, and let $\zeta$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The index set `extArithIndex S` is $\{*\}\sqcup S$, with local group the subgroup generated by complex conjugation at $*$ and the local Galois group of $q$ at $q\in S$, mapped to the global group by `extArithLoc`. Given, for each place $v$ in this set, a $\mathbb Z/p$-linear map $\theta_v$ from $\mathrm{continuousH}^1$ of the restriction of $M$ (the image under $H^1\pi$ of the level cocycles) into the dual of $\mathrm{continuousH}^1$ of the restriction of the dual twist $M^\vee\otimes\chi_p$ by the mod $p$ cyclotomic character; assume each $\theta_q$, $q\in S$, satisfies `IsTheta1` for the evaluation pairing into $\mathbb Z/p(\chi_p)$ and the invariant `localInv p ζ q`, i.e. it computes, on classes of level-constant cocycles, the value of that invariant on the class of any level $2$-cocycle agreeing with their cup cochain; assume likewise a $\mathbb Z/p$-functional $\mathrm{invInf}$ on $\mathrm{continuousH}^2$ at $*$, injective, with $\theta_*$ satisfying `IsTheta1` for it. Let $x\in\mathrm{continuousH}^1_S(M)$ and $y\in\mathrm{continuousH}^1_S(M^\vee\otimes\chi_p)$ (images of the $S$-level cocycles), and let $z_v,w_v$ be continuous local classes whose underlying $H^1$ classes are the restrictions `locRes` of $x$ and of $y$. Then $\sum_v \theta_v(z_v)(w_v)=0$.
--
--   This is the reciprocity half of Poitou–Tate exactness in degree one, stated at all places of $\{\infty\}\cup S$ for odd $p$: the local Tate pairings of two global classes sum to zero. It feeds the characterisation of which families of local classes come from a global class in the $S$-Selmer group, used in the two statements that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_groupCohomology_sum_theta1_locRes_eq_zero_of_mem_continuousH1S_arch_of_ne_two.lean

